/-
# Embedding residually finite locally normal groups (corrected variant of Kourovka Problem 6.8)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.8 (Yu. M. Gorchakov): can a residually
finite locally normal group be embedded in a Cartesian product of finite groups in such a way that
each element of the group has at most finitely many central projections? This module records only
a corrected variant, with finitely many *non-central* projections (Tomkinson's theorem); it does not
formalize Problem 6.8 as printed.
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.ResiduallyFinite
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ResiduallyFiniteLocallyNormalEmbeddingKourovka6Problem8Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.8 (Yu. M.
Gorchakov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700355 (`KOU-6.8`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A group is locally normal when every finite subset lies in a finite normal subgroup
(`IsLocallyNormal` of `GroupClassesShared`); residually finite is Mathlib's
`Group.ResiduallyFinite`. The Archive's text reads "at most finitely many central projections" (21st
issue, Archive, 6.8). Read literally, that condition fails for the identity unless there are only
finitely many factors (all projections of the identity are central), so it would allow only finite
groups, against the Archive's answer "Yes, it can". No erratum or primary formulation of 6.8 with
"non-central" has been located. The declarations below therefore state a corrected variant, not
Problem 6.8 as printed: each element has only finitely many *non-central* projections, which is the
recorded form of Tomkinson's theorem: the residually finite periodic FC-groups (exactly the
residually finite locally normal groups) are the subgroups of centrally restricted products of
finite groups, the subgroup of the Cartesian product generated by the restricted direct product and
the torsion subgroup of the centre (B. Hartley's zbMATH review of Tomkinson's monograph FC-groups
(1984), Zbl 0547.20031; L. A. Kurdachenko, Zbl 0598.20041, states the 1981 embedding); every element
of such a product has only finitely many non-central coordinates, and for periodic groups the two
conditions agree. The product is the unrestricted product `(i : ι) → F i` of finite groups indexed
by an arbitrary type.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared (IsLocallyNormal)

/-- The corrected (non-central) variant of Kourovka 6.8 (Yu. M. Gorchakov), after Tomkinson: every
residually finite locally normal group `G` embeds in a Cartesian product `∏ i, F i` of finite groups
so that every element of `G` has only finitely many coordinates outside the centre of the
corresponding factor. Problem 6.8 as printed asks for finitely many central projections instead. -/
def residuallyFiniteLocallyNormalNonCentralEmbedding : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], IsLocallyNormal G → Group.ResiduallyFinite G →
    ∃ (ι : Type) (F : ι → Type) (_ : ∀ i, Group (F i)) (_ : ∀ i, Finite (F i))
      (f : G →* ((i : ι) → F i)), Function.Injective f ∧
        ∀ g : G, {i | f g i ∉ Subgroup.center (F i)}.Finite

/--
Resolved true for the corrected (non-central) variant only; Problem 6.8 as printed, with finitely
many central projections, is not formalized here. The Kourovka Archive answers 6.8 "Yes, it can",
citing Tomkinson (1981). As recorded in zbMATH (Zbl 0547.20031, Zbl 0598.20041), every residually
finite periodic FC-group embeds in a centrally restricted product of finite groups (generated by the
restricted direct product and the torsion subgroup of the centre of the Cartesian product), in which
each element has only finitely many non-central coordinates. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov
(eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49
(2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 6.8 (Yu. M. Gorchakov); resolution: M. J. Tomkinson, A
characterization of residually finite periodic FC-groups, Bull. London Math. Soc. 13 (1981),
133-137, Kourovka Archive, Problem 6.8: Yes, it can (Tomkinson); theorem as recorded in zbMATH Zbl
0547.20031 (B. Hartley's review of Tomkinson, FC-groups, 1984) and Zbl 0598.20041,
https://doi.org/10.1112/blms/13.2.133.
-/
public theorem_wanted residuallyFiniteLocallyNormalNonCentralEmbedding_holds :
    residuallyFiniteLocallyNormalNonCentralEmbedding

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ResiduallyFiniteLocallyNormalEmbeddingKourovka6Problem8Wanted
